From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 16:17:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 21/30] Solver: twins, cleanfirst, lookahead (result-preserving
 speed-ups of overload resolution)

twins: candidates of one overload set that have the same type share one
exploration. cleanfirst: look for a solution without diagnostics first, with
the bound 'no error' from the start; fall back to the existing search if the
first overload set has no clean candidate. lookahead: during that search,
abandon a branch when a pending goal with closed types is certain to fail.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Mythos 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
